    <miscellaneous>
      <miscellaneous-field name="analysis-json">{"meta":{"id":"chopin_op28_suffocation","parent_item_id":"chopin_op28_suffocation","title":"Prelude: Op. 28, No. 4 ('Suffocation')","composer":"Frédéric Chopin","source_file":"files/scores/chopin_op28_suffocation.mid","quarter_range":[0,101.0],"bar_quarters":4.0,"pickup_quarters":1.0,"time_signature":"2/2","key":"e","tempo":56.0,"midi_play_url":"files/scores/chopin_op28_suffocation.mid","source_licence":"PD","source_page":"https://www.mutopiaproject.org/cgibin/piece-info.cgi?id=468","quantisation_divisors":[4,8,3],"notation_notes":"Mutopia MIDI (PD edition, piece 468): one-quarter pickup at quarter 0, bar 1 at quarter 1, 25 bars of 2/2 (4 quarters each) to quarter 101. No repeats. MIDI tempo 56 per quarter throughout. Pickup sounds B3 (dotted eighth) then B4 (sixteenth); printed editions show a B4 upbeat, so the B3 may be a source octave error. Bars 12 and 18 contain RH eighth-note triplets. Bar 23 has two quarters of sound then silence (the printed fermata rest). A# / D# are spelled Bb / Eb in the MIDI-derived score. The LH repeated chords and the final three chords are merged in places by the MIDI; the final bar is a single whole-bar chord. MIDI-derived score, not an Urtext.","suggested_arrangement_tempo":56,"sustain_events":[{"quarter":1.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":4.0,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":5.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":6.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":7.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":8.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":9.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":10.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":13.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":14.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":17.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":18.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":21.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":22.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":23.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":24.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":25.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":28.0,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":29.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":30.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":39.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":40.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":41.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":42.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":43.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":44.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":49.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":52.0,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":53.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":54.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":55.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":56.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":59.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":60.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":65.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":66.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":70.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":70.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":73.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":74.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":77.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":78.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":79.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":80.5,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":81.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":84.0,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":87.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":88.5,"channel":1,"value":0}]},"draft":false,"reviewed_by":"claude-opus-5-5 (MusicBot) 2026-10-11","summary":"E minor throughout, in two parallel halves (1–12, 13–25). Over a static B–C sigh in the melody, the LH repeated chords slide down one semitone at a time through dominant, half-diminished and diminished sevenths, reaching iv (A minor) by bar 9 and ending the first half on V7 (bar 12). The second half repeats the opening with a faster slide, breaks into the only climax (C6 over B7♭9, bar 17), dodges the cadence with V7 → VI (bars 20–21), and closes with an augmented sixth (bar 23) and V → i (bars 24–25). There are no real modulations; A minor is only tonicized.","sections":[{"name":"Upbeat","start_bar":0,"end_bar":0,"mood":["hushed"],"description":"Lone B upbeat."},{"name":"A (first half)","start_bar":1,"end_bar":12,"mood":["desolate","numb","sighing"],"description":"Melody holds B–C for four bars, then A–B, while the LH descends chromatically from i6 to iv6 (bar 9). Bars 9–12: the melody starts moving; B7 ↔ iv6 alternation; HC on V7 in bar 12."},{"name":"A′ (second half)","start_bar":13,"end_bar":16,"mood":["desolate","restless"],"description":"Restatement of bar 1 with a compressed chromatic slide (bars 14–15), then the melody breaks upward in bar 16."},{"name":"Climax and collapse","start_bar":17,"end_bar":20,"mood":["anguished","exhausted"],"description":"C6 over B7(b9) in bar 17, falling back at once; suspended dominants (bars 18–20) end on B7."},{"name":"Coda","start_bar":21,"end_bar":25,"mood":["resigned","grave","still"],"description":"Deceptive V7 → VI (bar 21), cadential 6/4 (bar 22), augmented sixth then silence (bar 23), V with 4–3 (bar 24), tonic close (bar 25)."}],"tricks":["Bars 1–8: the melody barely moves (B–C, then A–B); all the motion is in the LH chords, where one voice at a time slips down a semitone.","Bars 2–8: the chromatic slide passes through V43, a French-sixth-sounding B7♭5, iiø7 and viio7 colours before landing on iv6 at bar 9.","Bar 12: the LH drops out and the RH alone spells V7, ending the first half on the dominant.","Bar 17: the only climax, C6 over B7♭9 with an octave B bass, gone within a bar.","Bars 20–21: V7 → VI deceptive resolution delays the ending.","Bar 23: augmented sixth with A# in the bass, followed by silence, before V (with 4–3) → i."],"loop_candidates":[{"start_bar":1,"end_bar":8,"why":"Static B–C / A–B melody over a slowly descending chord bed; bar 8 G#o7 moves to A minor, so the seam back to bar 1 Em/G is audible.","quarter_range":[1,33],"requires_audition":true},{"start_bar":1,"end_bar":4,"why":"i6 → V43 → chromatic → E7 four-bar cell with a constant melody note; loops on a single held B.","quarter_range":[1,17],"requires_audition":true}],"hook_candidates":[{"start_bar":0,"end_bar":4,"why":"B upbeat, held B with C neighbour, LH chords sliding down: the recognisable opening.","quarter_range":[0,17]},{"start_bar":16,"end_bar":17,"why":"Melody leaps to A5 and peaks on C6 over B7♭9.","quarter_range":[61,69]},{"start_bar":20,"end_bar":25,"why":"Deceptive cadence, augmented sixth, silence and the final cadence.","quarter_range":[77,101]}],"kpop_uses":[{"where":"verse","why":"Bars 1–8 as a sparse piano bed; the near-static melody leaves room for a vocal line, and the LH chord slide gives slow harmonic motion."},{"where":"bridge","why":"Bars 16–17: the sudden upward break to C6 suits a short emotional peak before a drop-out."},{"where":"pre-chorus","why":"Bars 9–12: moving melody over B7 ↔ iv6, ending on V7 to set up a chorus in E minor."},{"where":"chorus","why":"Bars 20–25 as an outro: deceptive V7 → VI, a silent beat, then V → i. Slow (quarter = 56); no key change exists in the source."}],"review_flags":[{"bar":0,"reason":"Draft had no pickup, so all its bars were one quarter early and it showed 26 bars; corrected to a 1-quarter pickup + 25 bars (quarter range 0–101)."},{"bar":0,"reason":"Pickup B3 dotted-eighth + B4 sixteenth in the MIDI; editions print a B4 upbeat. Not corrected (MIDI kept as source)."},{"bar":1,"reason":"Draft key changes e → a (bar 1), a → E (bar 9), E → e (bar 17) removed: no cadence confirms either key. A minor is tonicized in bars 3–9; the piece stays in E minor."},{"bar":3,"reason":"Many LH sonorities in bars 2–8 and 14–16 are voice-leading products of the chromatic descent; the seventh-chord labels describe the sound, and the Roman numerals are approximate."},{"bar":3,"reason":"Beat 4 G#o7/F fails the check: B4 stops at beat 4 and the melody C5 is the recurring upper neighbour, so B is absent for one quarter (F–G#–D–C). Kept as G#o7; not relabelled Dø7."},{"bar":16,"reason":"Beat 3 left as ?: C#–E–Bb with A5 in the melody and no G; incomplete A7(b9)/C# or C#o7 with an appoggiatura."},{"bar":17,"reason":"Beat 3 (D#/F#/G/B for one eighth) is treated as the B7 resolving late; Em/G is labelled from beat 3.5."},{"bar":18,"reason":"Bsus4 in bars 18–20 has no D# until bar 20 beat 3; it could also be read as an Em/B 6/4 without G."},{"bar":21,"reason":"C7 on beat 3 has Bb moving down to A, so it is read as a chromatic VI7, not an augmented sixth; only bar 23 is labelled Ger+6."},{"bar":21,"reason":"Beat 1 C fails on coverage (66.7%): the MIDI pedal goes down on the same tick (q 81) as the bar-20 B7 chord releases, so the verifier holds B, D# and A into bar 21. The attacks are C3–G3–E4 only; C is kept."},{"bar":22,"reason":"Beat 1 B–E–A is read as Esus4/B (cadential 6/4 with suspended A), not B7sus4: no F# sounds."},{"bar":22,"reason":"G# on beat 2 is read as a passing major-mode colour in the A–G#–G inner line, not a real E-major arrival."},{"bar":25,"reason":"Printed editions have three separate final chords; the MIDI sounds one whole-bar chord. Dynamics (smorzando / pp) are not inferred."}],"schema_version":1,"bars":[{"bar":0,"start_quarter":0,"duration_quarters":1.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"?","rn":"?","function":"melodic upbeat","reason":"Lone B3 then B4; no harmony sounds."}],"events":[{"type":"story","technique":"start","text":"start: a lone B upbeat over silence; the long sigh begins"}]},{"bar":1,"start_quarter":1,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"Em/G","rn":"i6","function":"tonic, first inversion"}],"events":[{"type":"hook","technique":"melodic_cell","text":"B4 held, then C5 neighbour on beat 4: the two-note sigh that runs through bars 1–8"},{"type":"bass_line","technique":"chromatic","text":"Repeated-chord LH starts a slow chromatic descent: bass G3 (b1) → F#3 (b2) → F3 (b3) → E3 (b4) → Eb3 (b6) → D3 (b7)"},{"type":"voicing_orchestration","technique":"close_spacing","text":"LH eighth-note chords in close position; one voice slips by a semitone at a time"}]},{"bar":2,"start_quarter":5,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"B7sus4/F#","rn":"V43sus4","function":"dominant with E suspended"},{"beat":3,"symbol":"B7/F#","rn":"V43","function":"dominant seventh"}],"events":[{"type":"tension_release","technique":"suspension_4_3","text":"Inner E4 (held from bar 1) resolves to D#4","beat":3}]},{"bar":3,"start_quarter":9,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"B7b5/F","rn":"V43(b5)","function":"chromatic passing sonority (French-sixth sound; Fr+6 of A minor)"},{"beat":3,"symbol":"Bm7b5/F","rn":"iiø7/iv","function":"passing; A minor colour"},{"beat":4,"symbol":"G#o7/F","rn":"viio7/iv","function":"leading-tone seventh of A minor"}],"events":[{"type":"colour_chord","technique":"aug6_french","text":"F–A–B–D# under B4: French-sixth sound created by the chromatic LH descent, not a functional aug6 in E minor"}]},{"bar":4,"start_quarter":13,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"E7","rn":"V7/iv","function":"applied dominant of A minor"},{"beat":3,"symbol":"Em7","rn":"i7","function":"tonic seventh"},{"beat":4,"symbol":"C#o7/E","rn":"viio7/V (A#=Bb)","function":"common-tone diminished; melody Bb4 = A#"}],"events":[{"type":"rhythm_phrase","technique":"phrase_length","text":"Melody stays on B for four bars; the first change of note (Bb4 → A4) comes only at bar 4–5","beat":4}]},{"bar":5,"start_quarter":17,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"Am7/E","rn":"iv43","function":"subdominant seventh"},{"beat":3,"symbol":"F#ø7/E","rn":"iiø42","function":"predominant"}],"events":[{"type":"story","technique":"continuation","text":"continuation: the melody sinks a step to A while the harmony keeps sliding down"}]},{"bar":6,"start_quarter":21,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"F#ø7/E","rn":"iiø42","function":"predominant"},{"beat":3,"symbol":"D#o7","rn":"viio7","function":"leading-tone seventh"}],"events":[]},{"bar":7,"start_quarter":25,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"D7","rn":"V7/III","function":"applied dominant of G; not resolved"}],"events":[{"type":"tension_release","technique":"delayed_resolution","text":"D7 (V7 of G major) slides to Dm7 instead of resolving"}]},{"bar":8,"start_quarter":29,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"Dm7","rn":"iv7/iv","function":"chromatic passing"},{"beat":3,"symbol":"G#o7/D","rn":"viio7/iv","function":"leading-tone seventh of A minor"}],"events":[]},{"bar":9,"start_quarter":33,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"Am/C","rn":"iv6","function":"subdominant"}],"events":[{"type":"tension_release","technique":"suspension_7_6","text":"LH B3 over C3 (a 7th) falls to A3 on beat 2"},{"type":"texture_dynamics","technique":"thickening","text":"Melody turns from held notes to a moving eighth-note line (A–B–D–C–E–A)","beat":2},{"type":"story","technique":"turn","text":"turn: the frozen melody starts moving for the first time"}]},{"bar":10,"start_quarter":37,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"B7sus4","rn":"V7sus4","function":"dominant with E suspended"},{"beat":2,"symbol":"B7","rn":"V7","function":"dominant seventh"},{"beat":3,"symbol":"F#ø7/C","rn":"iiø43","function":"predominant"},{"beat":4,"symbol":"Am/C","rn":"iv6","function":"subdominant"}],"events":[{"type":"tension_release","technique":"suspension_4_3","text":"LH E3 resolves to D#3","beat":2}]},{"bar":11,"start_quarter":41,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"B7","rn":"V7","function":"dominant seventh"},{"beat":3,"symbol":"F#ø7/C","rn":"iiø43","function":"predominant"},{"beat":4,"symbol":"Am/C","rn":"iv6","function":"subdominant"}],"events":[{"type":"motif","technique":"repetition","text":"Bars 10–11 repeat the F#4 held note and B7 → iv6 alternation"}]},{"bar":12,"start_quarter":45,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"B7","rn":"V7","function":"dominant; arpeggiated by the RH alone after beat 1"}],"events":[{"type":"texture_dynamics","technique":"thinning","text":"LH drops out after beat 1; the RH alone outlines B7 with C and G neighbours"},{"type":"cadence","technique":"HC","text":"First half ends on V7 (bars 1–12)"},{"type":"rhythm_phrase","technique":"elision","text":"The triplet D5–C5–B4 on beat 4 is the upbeat into the return at bar 13","beat":4}]},{"bar":13,"start_quarter":49,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"Em/G","rn":"i6","function":"tonic, first inversion"}],"events":[{"type":"form","technique":"theme_1","text":"Bar 13 restates bar 1 (melody and LH)"},{"type":"story","technique":"continuation","text":"continuation: the opening sigh returns, but its chromatic slide moves faster"}]},{"bar":14,"start_quarter":53,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"B7sus4/F#","rn":"V43sus4","function":"dominant with E suspended"},{"beat":3,"symbol":"B7b5/F","rn":"V43(b5)","function":"chromatic passing sonority (French-sixth sound)"}],"events":[{"type":"rhythm_phrase","technique":"phrase_length","text":"The descent of bars 2–4 is compressed: the bar-3 sonority now arrives on beat 3 of bar 14"}]},{"bar":15,"start_quarter":57,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"Fø7","rn":"passing","function":"chromatic passing sonority (E#ø7 enharmonic)"},{"beat":2,"symbol":"G#o7/F","rn":"viio7/iv","function":"leading-tone seventh of A minor"},{"beat":3,"symbol":"E7","rn":"V7/iv","function":"applied dominant of A minor"}],"events":[]},{"bar":16,"start_quarter":61,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"Em7","rn":"i7","function":"tonic seventh"},{"beat":2,"symbol":"C#o7/E","rn":"viio7/V","function":"common-tone diminished"},{"beat":3,"symbol":"?","rn":"?","function":"chromatic passing","reason":"C#3–E3–Bb3 under A5: A(b9)/C# or C#o7 with A appoggiatura; no G or A in the LH, so neither reading is complete."},{"beat":4,"symbol":"F#ø7/C","rn":"iiø43","function":"predominant"}],"events":[{"type":"texture_dynamics","technique":"build_to_climax","text":"RH breaks out of the B–C sigh: Bb4 then a leap to A5 and F#5–E5"},{"type":"voicing_orchestration","technique":"register_high_shift","text":"Melody jumps from B4 to A5, the highest point so far","beat":3}]},{"bar":17,"start_quarter":65,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"B7b9","rn":"V7(b9)","function":"dominant with flat ninth; B octave bass held by pedal"},{"beat":3.5,"symbol":"Em/G","rn":"i6","function":"tonic, first inversion"}],"events":[{"type":"texture_dynamics","technique":"climax","text":"C6 over B7(b9) is the melodic peak; octave B1–B2 is the lowest bass so far","beat":2},{"type":"tension_release","technique":"appoggiatura","text":"E5 over B7 falls to D#5 (Eb5 in the MIDI)"},{"type":"story","technique":"turn","text":"turn: the only outburst; the line peaks at C6 and falls straight back"}]},{"bar":18,"start_quarter":69,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"Am","rn":"iv","function":"subdominant"},{"beat":2.5,"symbol":"F#ø7/A","rn":"iiø65","function":"predominant"},{"beat":3,"symbol":"Bsus4","rn":"Vsus4","function":"dominant with unresolved 4th"},{"beat":4,"symbol":"F#ø7/C","rn":"iiø43","function":"predominant"}],"events":[{"type":"texture_dynamics","technique":"thinning","text":"Climax collapses: melody falls through E5–E4–A4 to a held F#4"}]},{"bar":19,"start_quarter":73,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"Bsus4","rn":"Vsus4","function":"dominant with unresolved 4th"},{"beat":3,"symbol":"F#ø7/C","rn":"iiø43","function":"predominant"},{"beat":4,"symbol":"Am/C","rn":"iv6","function":"subdominant"}],"events":[{"type":"motif","technique":"repetition","text":"Bar 19 = bar 11 melody over a suspended dominant"}]},{"bar":20,"start_quarter":77,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"e","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"Bsus4","rn":"Vsus4","function":"dominant with 4th"},{"beat":3,"symbol":"B","rn":"V","function":"dominant"},{"beat":4,"symbol":"B7","rn":"V7","function":"dominant seventh"}],"events